From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: kernelbase, shell32: app execution aliases

A package's windows.appExecutionAlias (winget.exe, python.exe, a Store
app's command) is on Windows an IO_REPARSE_TAG_APPEXECLINK reparse point
in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\WindowsApps that CreateProcess follows to the
package's executable. appxdeploymentclient (next patch) writes the alias
as a small text file instead, described in wine/appexeclink.h:
PackageFamilyName, AppUserModelId, Target.

- CreateProcess starts the target in the alias's place, keeping the
  caller's command line -- only when the target is inside the install
  location of a package of that family deployed for the user, so a
  planted file cannot redirect anything.
- SHGetFileInfo(SHGFI_EXETYPE) reports the target's type, so cmd.exe
  waits for a console program started through its alias and gets its exit
  code.

